# Vercel Blob / `file_asset` (Pulse)

**Normative guide:** [`docs/guidelines/nextjs/blob-upload-agent-instruction.md`](docs/guidelines/nextjs/blob-upload-agent-instruction.md)  
**Schema:** [`database_schema_v1.md`](docs/prds/03_data_model/database_schema_v1.md) — `file_asset`, `file_upload_status`

## Required alignment

- **Single registry:** Prisma **`FileAsset`** only (`blob_pathname`, `blob_url`, `upload_status`, …). No parallel file tables.
- **Lifecycle:** **`pending`** row with server-chosen pathname → client upload to Vercel Blob → server verify → **`ready`** or **`failed`**. Link FKs (certificates, profile photos) only after **`ready`**.
- **Auth and policy:** `auth()` + `@pulse/policy-server` on every upload mutation.
- **Reads:** serve or sign URLs only when **`upload_status = ready`**; do not persist expiring URLs as source of truth.
- **Paths:** code under `apps/web/src/`; Prisma via `@pulse/db`.
- **Next.js 16:** Server Actions vs Route Handlers per [ai_nextjs_db_data_handle.md](docs/guidelines/nextjs/ai_nextjs_db_data_handle.md); cache: `updateTag` / `revalidateTag` per ADR-002.

## Storage (ADR-001)

- **Vercel Blob** — not S3. Env: `BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN` (server-only).

Reference: lampto `s3-file-asset-uploads.mdc` — adapted for Vercel Blob + Pulse schema.
